{
  "$comment": [
    "Event-topic pattern conformance table. One grammar: a topic is dot-separated segments (the text between two dots, so empty segments exist); in a pattern, `*` is exactly one whole segment, `**` is zero or more whole segments, anything else is literal. A pattern equal to the topic always matches.",
    "Columns are the surfaces that use the grammar, each through a stated projection:",
    "  grammar      - the grammar exactly.",
    "  subscription - plugin consumes.events, delivery, the SDK pattern listeners: the grammar exactly, `**` included.",
    "  declaration  - plugin provides.events: the grammar without `**`, which is a literal segment there.",
    "  live         - /v1/events/live?include=: the grammar plus a within-segment glob (`write_*`) that never crosses a dot. Plugin events are named `plugin.<event_type>` on that stream.",
    "  stage        - a stage's Capability.emits / consumes: the declaration rules, except that a trailing `.*` covers one or more segments.",
    "Every consumer's tests run the columns that apply to it. The plugin SDKs keep byte-identical copies of this file; change a row only together with the matcher, every consumer, and the copies (`just sync-topic-table`)."
  ],
